Subject: [candle] metal-stream-and-buffer-pool-seam

  The stream machinery OSCAR drives its own encoder scopes through, the command-buffer observer, and THE SEAM EVERY METAL BUFFER COMES THROUGH: candle asks an installed pool for every allocation and has no path to the driver beside it, naming which pool a request belongs to, the queue whose free lists serve it, the fence a buffer the CPU writes into is reused behind, the fence a freed buffer's PAGES go back to the OS on (which an idle queue can only ever meet the second way), the LINE OF CODE a host fill came from — the tensor constructors are `#[track_caller]` down to the seam, so the pool holds the caller's own location as the buffer's label where there is no kernel to name it — and the one call a model build places a weight it KEEPS through — the floor, from host bytes, refusing a device source.

Applies to: 0.10.2
Files: 18

